            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous vs surgical placement of intra-aortic balloon assist.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>519-23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fifty-three patients required IABP over a one-year period. The type of insertion (percutaneous vs surgical) was used randomly. The hemodynamic effect, complication rate, and inability to insert the balloon were similar in both groups. Besides less trauma and cost-effectiveness, the most important advantage of percutaneous over surgical balloon insertion is shorter time interval between decision and insertion which thus allows faster stabilization of ischemic heart patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
